	(text "Tap point: digital RGB bus going INTO the Marty downscaler ASIC (between the CRTC and the downscaler).\nReverse-engineering state (Jun 2025): HSYNC + blanking + field signals are localised; exact R/G/B pin positions are still being\nmapped via colour-gradient probing. See https://github.com/ottj/FM-Towns-Marty-Reverse-Engineering — `marty asic.xlsx`.\n\nWiring on the Marty side: flying leads from test pads through the IC card slot opening to a 2x16 IDC header (J2).\nLevels at J2 are 5V CMOS. 74LVC16245A x2 translate to +3V3 for FPGA. DIR tied +3V3 (always A->B, Marty->FPGA), ~OE tied GND.\n\nTODO before fab: per-signal 33R series-R + TVS array on J2 inputs (currently omitted for concept clarity)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50 200 0)
